:"blue","kme":0.551929,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.548873,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false},"mathys2019":{"dataset_label":"Mathys et al. 2019","gene_ids":["ENSG00000156313"],"dataset_symbols":["RPGR"],"explorer":"explorer.html?dataset=mathys2019#gene/RPGR","cell_types":[{"cell_type":"Ex","gene_symbol":"RPGR","gene_symbol_current":"RPGR","gene_id":"ENSG00000156313","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":false,"nucleus_direction":"unclear","nucleus_padj":0.614672,"nucleus_log2fc":0.0403184,"nucleus_score":-0.606416,"pct_ad":0.133076,"pct_control":0.136784,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.998051,"donor_log2fc":0.00673965,"donor_lfcse":0.104263,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":1.48683e-06},{"cell_type":"In","gene_symbol":"RPGR","gene_symbol_current":"RPGR","gene_id":"ENSG00000156313","nucleus_tested":false,"nucleus_significant":null,"nucleus_direction":"not tested","nucleus_padj":null,"nucleus_log2fc":null,"nucleus_score":null,"pct_ad":null,"pct_control":null,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.999889,"donor_log2fc":0.0948612,"donor_lfcse":0.165036,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":3.56874e-06}],"modules":[],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000156313","entrez_id":["6103"],"uniprot":["Q92834"],"ncbi_summary":"This gene encodes a protein with a series of six RCC1-like domains (RLDs), characteristic of the highly conserved guanine nucleotide exchange factors. The encoded protein is found in the Golgi body and interacts with RPGRIP1. This protein localizes to the outer segment of rod photoreceptors and is essential for their viability. Mutations in this gene have been associated with X-linked retinitis pigmentosa (XLRP). Multiple alternatively spliced transcript variants that encode different isoforms of this gene have been reported, but the full-length natures of only some have been determined. [provided by RefSeq, Dec 2008].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q92834","text":"Acts as a guanine-nucleotide releasing factor (GEF) for RAB8A and RAB37 by promoting the conversion of inactive RAB-GDP to the active form RAB-GTP (PubMed:20631154). GEF activity towards RAB8A may facilitate ciliary trafficking by modulating ciliary intracellular localization of RAB8A (PubMed:20631154). GEF activity towards RAB37 maintains autophagic homeostasis and retinal function (By similarity). Involved in photoreceptor integrity (By similarity). May control cilia formation by regulating actin stress filaments and cell contractility. May be involved in microtubule organization and regulation of transport in primary cilia (PubMed:21933838). May play a critical role in spermatogenesis and in intraflagellar transport processes (By similarity)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}